1. Observability Architecture Overview:
--------------------------------------
Components:
Application Pods / ECS Tasks
       │
       │ emits metrics, logs, traces
       ▼
  OpenTelemetry Collector (OTel)
       │
 ┌─────┴─────┐
 │           │
Metrics    Traces / Logs
 │           │
 ▼           ▼
New Relic Metrics API / Logs API
       │
 Dashboards, Alerts, and Analytics

*OpenTelemetry (OTel) collects metrics, logs, and traces from all services (EKS Pods / ECS Tasks / CI/CD pipelines).
*New Relic receives structured data, aggregates it, and provides dashboards and alerts.
*Tenant-specific metrics are tagged with namespace or tenant ID.
*Pipeline performance metrics (build time, deployment success/failure) are exported as custom events.

Metrics Collection:
-------------------
Resources tracks:
1.System metrics: CPU, memory, disk, network for Pods/ECS tasks, nodes.
2.Application metrics: Request rate, latency, error rate, queue depth, DB connections.
3.Pipeline metrics: Build duration, success/failure, artifact storage usage.
4.Tenant-specific metrics: Namespace-level resource usage, requests per tenant.

Step1:Deploy OTel Collector via Helm:
-------------------------------------
helm repo add open-telemetry https://open-telemetry.github.io/opentelemetry-helm-charts
helm install otel-collector open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector \
  --namespace observability \
  --set config.receiver.otlp.protocols.grpc.endpoint="0.0.0.0:4317" \
  --set config.exporter.newrelic.api_key="<NEW_RELIC_API_KEY>" \
  --set config.exporter.newrelic.metrics_endpoint="https://metric-api.newrelic.com"

