Data Export & Analysis Structure:
---------------------------------

Metrics: OTLP → OTel Collector → New Relic Metrics API
Logs: stdout → Fluent Bit → OTel Collector → New Relic Logs API
Traces: OpenTelemetry SDK → Collector → New Relic Trace API

1.Labels/Tags for structured analysis:

  tenant_id → multi-tenant isolation
  namespace → Kubernetes namespace
  service_name → EKS/ECS service
  environment → production/staging
  pipeline_id → CI/CD correlation
  request_id → trace correlation

2.This structure allows:

Tenant-level SLA monitoring
Cross-service latency analysis
Pipeline bottleneck detection
Alerting on critical events

Security & Best Practices:
--------------------------
OTel Collector runs in private subnets with restricted Security Groups.
API keys (New Relic) stored in AWS Secrets Manager or Kubernetes Secrets.
TLS encryption in transit for logs/metrics/traces.
RBAC controls which teams can access dashboards/alerts.
Rate limits & filters on OTel Collector to prevent noisy tenants from overloading observability pipeline.
